@startuml hld-01a_layer_map
title HLD-01a — Layer map, HIGH VIEW (UML **package diagram**)\nDependencies are UML package dependencies: «import» = public import, «access» = private import (UML 2.5 §12.2).\nWhich module depends on which, through which interface, is HLD-01b.
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 200

package shell <<Composition Root>> #LightGray {
}
package modules <<Bounded Contexts>> #Gold {
}
package support <<Generic Subdomains>> #White {
}
package core <<Application Kernel>> #LightGray {
  package "core.contracts" <<Contracts>>
  package "core.vo" <<Published Language>>
}
package sagittarius_engine <<Framework>> #WhiteSmoke {
}

shell ..> modules : <<access>>
shell ..> "core.contracts" : <<import>>
shell ..> sagittarius_engine : <<import>>
modules ..> modules : <<access>>
modules ..> support : <<import>>
modules ..> "core.contracts" : <<import>>
modules ..> "core.vo" : <<import>>
support ..> "core.vo" : <<import>>
"core.contracts" ..> sagittarius_engine : <<import>>

note right of modules
  **modules** — one nested package per bounded context:
  strategy <<Core Domain>>, market_data <<Supporting>>,
  trading <<Supporting>>, backtesting <<Supporting>>.
  The «access» dependency on itself is the module-to-module
  rule: a module may reach another module's `contracts`
  sub-package and nothing else. It is acyclic — HLD-01b
  draws each edge of it.
end note

note bottom of shell
  **shell** is Martin's *Main* component: the only package that
  names every module (`modules.py`, explicit and topologically
  ordered), owns `surfaces/` and assembles the CLI parser.
end note

note bottom of support
  **support** — binance_gateway (the only constructor of
  `binance.client.Client`), charting, indicators, ui_kit.
  No business language, so in principle buyable.
end note

note bottom of "core.vo"
  `core.vo` is a **Published Language**, not a Shared Kernel:
  the Shared Kernel is exactly two Engine types, IDomainEvent
  and BaseEvent, and a test locks that definition. A type enters
  `core.vo` only with ≥ 2 consumers in ≥ 2 modules.
end note

note top of sagittarius_engine
  No dependency points back up: `core` never imports `modules`
  or `support`, the Engine never imports the application, and no
  module imports `shell`. The guard `test_module_boundaries.py`
  (§6) enforces exactly the dependencies drawn here.
end note
@enduml
